# Regression: an error must be charged to the script that caused it.
#
# The `fail_` prefix means the runner expects exactly this script to fail, so
# it goes red both ways: if the error is misattributed this script reports a
# false pass, and whichever script it leaked into goes red instead.
#
# Two things used to break that. A script's own `reset_test_state` doubled as
# the runner's internal script separator, so it ended the script early and
# shifted every later result by one. And the last command was finalized in the
# same tick it was dispatched, before it had run.

goto_screen virtual_list_lab
wait 0.3

# The separator case: this must reset input state without ending the script.
reset_test_state
wait 0.2

# The last-command case: this is the final command, and its failure still
# has to land here.
expect_text "deliberately absent, this script is meant to fail"
